-- Q11787: State and Local Government [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB 34, paragraphs 37-40, program revenues include charges for services ($1.1M in fines and fees) and operating/capital grants ($400K federal grant), totaling $1.5M. Property taxes ($7.1M) are general revenues that fund remaining net expenses across all functions.
Wrong (A): Property taxes are always general revenues under GASB 34, regardless of internal allocation. Only $1.5M qualifies as program revenue.
Wrong (B): Property taxes are classified as general revenues even when earmarked to a specific department. Internal budget allocation does not change the GASB classification.
Wrong (D): Fines and fees are charges for services, which are a category of program revenue under GASB 34, not excluded as exchange transactions.$EXPL$
