  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB 34, paragraph 130, the budgetary comparison schedule must present the original budget, the final amended budget, and actual results for the general fund and major special revenue funds. Both budget columns allow users to evaluate the significance of mid-year amendments.
Wrong (B): Omitting the original budget prevents users from assessing whether amendments reflect sound fiscal management. GASB 34 requires both columns.
Wrong (C): Budget amounts must appear as separate columns in the schedule, not merely in footnotes. The comparison format is required, not optional.
Wrong (D): The final amended budget is equally required so users can compare actuals against the final authorized spending level.$EXPL$
