-- Q11793: Income Taxes [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25-47 and ASC 718-10-25, a DTA is recognized as compensation cost is recorded for book purposes, even though the tax deduction occurs at exercise. The DTA equals cumulative book expense times the enacted rate: $100,000 x 21% = $21,000.
Wrong (A): $63,000 incorrectly applies 21% to the full $300,000 grant-date fair value rather than the $100,000 of expense recognized in Year 1.
Wrong (B): $100,000 confuses the book compensation expense with the deferred tax asset. The DTA is the expense multiplied by the tax rate, not the expense itself.
Wrong (C): A DTA of $0 is incorrect because ASC 740 requires recognition of a DTA as book expense is recorded, not deferred until the tax deduction becomes available.$EXPL$
