Wrong (A): $29,400 incorrectly applies 21% to the $140,000 already paid. Amounts paid have been deducted for both book and tax and are no longer a temporary difference.
Wrong (C): $67,200 appears to apply an incorrect rate or base amount. The temporary difference is only the $180,000 year-end accrual.
