-- Q11798: Income Taxes [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25-20, GAAP expense of $500,000 exceeds the Year 1 tax deduction of $100,000, so taxable income exceeds book income by $400,000. This future deductible temporary difference produces a DTA of $400,000 x 21% = $84,000. The remaining $400,000 tax basis will generate future deductions.
Wrong (A): A DTL of $84,000 reverses the direction. Because more tax deductions will occur in future years, the difference creates future tax savings (DTA), not future tax obligations.
Wrong (B): $105,000 incorrectly applies 21% to the full $500,000 rather than the $400,000 temporary difference.
Wrong (C): A DTL of $105,000 is wrong in both direction and amount. The book-tax difference creates a DTA, not a DTL.$EXPL$
