Wrong (B): A DTA of $42,000 reverses the direction. Because the tax deduction was accelerated relative to book, a liability (not asset) arises for future taxable amounts.
Wrong (C): A DTL of $50,400 incorrectly applies 21% to the full $240,000 premium rather than the $200,000 temporary difference.
