  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the book impairment reduces the carrying amount ($350,000) below the tax basis ($700,000) by $350,000, creating a deductible temporary difference. The DTA is $350,000 x 21% = $73,500. The future tax deduction at disposal will exceed the remaining book basis.
Wrong (B): A DTL of $73,500 reverses the direction. Because book basis is below tax basis, future tax deductions will exceed book deductions, creating a DTA not a DTL.
Wrong (C): A DTA of $147,000 incorrectly applies 21% to the full $700,000 original carrying amount rather than the $350,000 temporary difference.
Wrong (D): Impairment losses that generate future tax deductions are temporary, not permanent, differences. The deduction is merely deferred until disposal.$EXPL$
