-- Q11807: Income Taxes [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25-9 and 740-10-35-2, when a previously unrecognized tax benefit meets the more-likely-than-not threshold, the liability is removed and the benefit reduces income tax expense in the current period. The entry debits the UTB liability and credits income tax expense for $84,000.
Wrong (A): Recognition flows through the income statement, not directly through retained earnings. Charging retained earnings would bypass the income statement entirely.
Wrong (B): Waiting for the statute of limitations to expire is unnecessary. Recognition occurs when the threshold is met, regardless of whether the statute has expired.
Wrong (C): Crediting cash is incorrect because recognizing a tax benefit does not involve a cash payment. The entry removes the liability against income tax expense.$EXPL$
