  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the $300,000 restructuring liability creates a deductible temporary difference because the expense is recognized for book in Year 1 but deductible for tax only when paid in Year 2. The DTA is $300,000 x 21% = $63,000.
Wrong (A): A DTL of $63,000 reverses the direction. Because the book expense precedes the tax deduction, a future deductible amount exists, creating a DTA not a DTL.
Wrong (C): Restructuring charges that will be tax-deductible when paid are temporary differences, not permanent ones. The deduction is deferred, not disallowed.
