-- Q11812: Income Taxes [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 740-10-25-20, the ROU asset (book $450,000, tax basis $0) creates a DTL of $94,500, while the lease liability (book $450,000, tax basis $0) creates an offsetting DTA of $94,500. At inception these net to zero. Over time, different amortization rates may create a net difference.
Wrong (A): A net DTL of $94,500 considers only the ROU asset without the offsetting DTA from the lease liability. Both must be considered together.
Wrong (B): A net DTA of $94,500 considers only the lease liability without the offsetting DTL from the ROU asset. The two temporary differences offset at inception.
Wrong (D): Operating leases do create book assets and liabilities under ASC 842 even though they remain off-balance-sheet for tax. Deferred tax recognition is required.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11812;

-- Q11813: Income Taxes [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 740-10-25-30, a DTA is recognized for NOL carryforwards at the enacted rate: $800,000 x 21% = $168,000. The 80% annual limitation restricts utilization per year but does not reduce the total DTA because the NOL carries forward indefinitely until fully used.
Wrong (B): $134,400 incorrectly applies the 80% cap to the DTA calculation ($800,000 x 80% x 21%). The cap is a timing constraint on utilization, not a reduction of the DTA.
Wrong (C): $800,000 confuses the NOL amount with the DTA. The DTA is the NOL multiplied by the tax rate, not the NOL itself.
Wrong (D): A DTA of $0 is incorrect because management expects sufficient future income to utilize the NOL. A valuation allowance is not needed when realization is more likely than not.$EXPL$
