-- Q11815: Income Taxes [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 740-10-25-30, tax credit carryforwards are recognized as DTAs at face value because credits reduce tax liability dollar-for-dollar, unlike NOL carryforwards which must be multiplied by the tax rate. The DTA equals the full $250,000 credit amount.
Wrong (A): Tax credits are assets (future tax reductions), not liabilities. Recording a liability of $250,000 mischaracterizes the nature of unused credits.
Wrong (B): Footnote-only disclosure is insufficient. ASC 740 requires recognition of a DTA for credit carryforwards when realization is more likely than not.
Wrong (C): A DTA of $52,500 incorrectly applies the 21% tax rate to the credits. Rate multiplication is appropriate for NOLs, not for tax credits which offset taxes dollar-for-dollar.$EXPL$
