-- Q11817: Income Taxes [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 740-10-25-20, recognizing $240,000 of profit for book while deferring it for tax creates a $240,000 taxable temporary difference. The DTL is $240,000 x 21% = $50,400 because the profit will be taxed upon contract completion.
Wrong (A): A DTA of $50,400 reverses the direction. Because book income exceeds taxable income, a future taxable amount exists, creating a DTL not a DTA.
Wrong (B): A DTL of $126,000 incorrectly applies 21% to the total $600,000 expected profit rather than the $240,000 recognized to date.
