-- Q11820: Not-for-Profit Accounting [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 958-210-45, board-designated funds are internally restricted by the governing board, not by donors. Because the board can reverse its own designation at any time, these amounts remain classified as net assets without donor restrictions.
Wrong (B): Net assets with donor restrictions require an external donor-imposed restriction. Board designations are internal and do not meet this criterion under ASC 958.
Wrong (C): ASC 958 recognizes only two categories of net assets: with and without donor restrictions. There is no separate third category for board designations.
Wrong (D): Board designations do not create liabilities. The funds remain net assets because no obligation to an external party exists.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11820;

-- Q11821: Not-for-Profit Accounting [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 958-605-25-24, when a recipient NFP has variance power--the unilateral ability to redirect transferred assets to another beneficiary--it is treated as a donee rather than an agent. Maplewood recognizes the $1,000,000 as contribution revenue because variance power indicates economic substance.
Wrong (A): Administrative fees are relevant to cost recovery but do not determine agent-versus-donee classification. Variance power is the controlling factor.
Wrong (C): Whether the beneficiary has been notified does not affect the accounting classification. The determinative factor is whether the intermediary holds variance power.
Wrong (D): The donor''s tax treatment is a tax law matter and does not affect how the recipient NFP classifies the transaction under ASC 958.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11821;

-- Q11822: Not-for-Profit Accounting [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 958-720-45-1, joint costs of activities that include a fundraising appeal may be allocated between fundraising and program functions only if the purpose, audience, and content criteria are all met. If any single criterion fails, the entire cost must be charged to fundraising.
Wrong (A): There is no revenue threshold requirement for joint cost allocation. The criteria are purpose, audience, and content--not financial return.
Wrong (B): ASC 958-720 does not require independent appraiser approval. Management applies the three criteria using its own judgment and supporting evidence.
Wrong (C): There is no minimum content percentage specified in the guidance. The content criterion evaluates whether a program function is served, not a quantitative threshold.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11822;
